# issue #47 star powers (bsrl-sim), a diff on top of the other patches (after repeat_masked.patch; first recorded on top of gears.patch, re-recorded on main b80459a).
# native/loader/starfx.c re-implements star power cards whose reader is compiled out of libg, from the card's own Value
# columns (card +0x110, Type enum card +0x100): damage taken (-V1 %, below an hp line, at full hp) and damage dealt (to a
# target at low hp, after a kill) in env.c my_root (before the gear shield), a kill hook in env.c record_event (R-T's linked hit too; every
# damage path ends there), double reload below an hp line (superfix_status.c my_reload_pct), a heal every V2 ticks and a
# move speed below an hp line (env.c hyper_tick / rec_move; an hp-line change re-sends the move). NbeResp star_valid /
# star_card / star_kind / star_stat (every response; nbenv_proto.h, py/nbpc/proto.py). NB_STAR_FX=0 turns the effects off;
# NB_STAR_VT=1 logs the calls of libg's lazy init 0xb2fe44 (the vtable probe of notes/issue47.md). build.sh: starfx.c.
# Notes: notes/issue47.md. Paths relative to engine/.
# Re-recorded for the linear chain (series): applies with -p1 on the tree the patches before it in series leave.
